## What are Closures?

Closures are a fundamental JavaScript concept where inner functions maintain access to variables from their outer (lexical) scope, even after the outer function completes execution.

## React Use Case

```javascript
function Counter({ initialCount }) {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);

  // This callback creates a closure over 'count'
  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    setCount(count + 1); // Accesses outer 'count' variable
  }, [count]);

  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Count: {count}</button>;
}
```

## Key Benefits

- Preserves access to outer scope variables
- Enables powerful patterns in React development
- Maintains state consistency across component re-renders
- Supports memoization and performance optimization

Closures enable functional patterns: private state, currying, and memoization. Trade-offs: closures keep references alive, increasing memory footprint; avoid capturing huge objects. Edge cases: loops with var can close over the wrong index; use let. In UIs, closures can lead to stale state if components re-render without updating bindings; debouncing/memoization illustrate how closures bind behavior to a specific creation context. Debounce example:
```
const debounce = (fn, wait) => {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), wait);
  };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to implement a real-world cache with per-key TTL, deduplicated async work, and a lightweight pub/sub hook using closures.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key state with closures
- Promise deduplication across concurrent callers
- TTL-based invalidation and manual refresh
- Simple pub/sub for updates without external libs

## Code Example
```javascript
function createNotificationCache(fetchFn, ttlMs) {
  const store = new Map();
  return {
    get(userId) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { data: null, inFlight: null, expiry: 0, listeners: [] };
      if (entry.inFlight) return entry.inFlight;
      const p = fetchFn(userId).then(d => {
        entry.data = d;
        entry.expiry = Date.now() + ttlMs;
        entry.inFlight = null;
        return d;
      }).catch(e => { entry.inFlight = null; throw e; });
      entry.inFlight = p;
      store.set(userId, entry);
      return p;
    },
    refresh(userId) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { inFlight: null };
      const p = fetchFn(userId).then(d => {
        entry.data = d; entry.expiry = Date.now() + ttlMs; entry.inFlight = null; return d;
      });
      entry.inFlight = p; store.set(userId, entry); return p;
    },
    onUpdate(userId, cb) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { listeners: [] };
      entry.listeners.push(cb);
      store.set(userId, entry);
      return () => {
        entry.listeners = entry.listeners.filter(x => x !== cb);
      };
    }
  };
}
```

